Kernel headers
--------------
Lineage 20 always generates the kernel UAPI headers (device_kernel_headers
is rewritten to generated_kernel_headers) by running headers_install on
TARGET_KERNEL_SOURCE, so the build needs kernel source even with a
prebuilt kernel. TARGET_FORCE_PREBUILT_KERNEL keeps kernel.mk from
building that source. libtinycompress is the user in this build.

The headers come from the 3.10 universal7420 kernel. headers_install runs
once with ARCH=arm64, and the 32-bit libtinycompress (for the 32-bit audio
HAL) also includes that asm/. The arm64 sigcontext.h in 6.6 uses
__uint128_t, which 32-bit clang does not have; the 3.10 tree defines its
own ___uint128_t struct instead. Add to .repo/local_manifests/ and repo
sync that path:

  <project path="kernel/samsung/universal7420" name="samsungexynos7420/android_kernel_samsung_universal7420" remote="github" revision="lineage-20.0-unify-clang-2" clone-depth="1" />

Built with 1de3d6e11448b14de2a6cd7dcc6f2ec94887d833. Moving to 6.6 UAPI
headers needs a 6.6 tree whose arm64 sigcontext.h builds for 32-bit.

Nothing in this checkout is compiled.
